    "result_text": "All tests pass \u2014 full suite: **64 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors** (BUILD SUCCESS).\n\n## Summary\n\nI redesigned the owner identity key and duplicate detection to match the new specification.\n\n### Identity key \u2014 now `SHA-256(normalizedTelephone | lowerEmail | soundex(lastName))`\n- **`Owner.getIdentityKey()`** (`model/Owner.java`) now returns the 64-char lower-case hex SHA-256 digest over the E.164 telephone, the lower-cased email (empty when absent), and the Soundex code of the last name \u2014 replacing the old plaintext `telephone|email|householdId` join. Added a private `sha256hex` helper.\n- **`model/Soundex.java`** (new): a self-contained American Soundex encoder (no new dependency), shared by the identity key and the soft-match.\n\n### Duplicate detection (409)\n- **`EnsureUniqueIdentity`** is unchanged in logic \u2014 it already compares the whole `identityKey`, ignores soft-deleted owners, and runs after the email-domain blocklist (which fires as a 400 during field validation, i.e. first). Only its Javadoc was updated.\n\n### Soft-match \u2014 now Soundex(lastName) + postcode with a differing identityKey\n- **`AssignPossibleDuplicate`** now flags a possible duplicate when the last names share a Soundex code, the postcodes match, and the full `identityKey` differs (previously it keyed on literal last name + postcode + differing telephone).\n\n### Household-duplicate 409 block removed\nBecause the telephone is part of the key, two owners with the same last name and postcode but different telephones are now a soft match, not a hard duplicate. I removed the separate household-duplicate block entirely:\n- Dropped the `ensureUniqueHousehold` step from `owners.POST.yml` (now `assignHousehold \u2192 ensureUniqueIdentity`).\n- Deleted `EnsureUniqueHousehold`, `HouseholdDuplicateException`, `HouseholdDuplicateExceptionHandler`, and its escalation YAML.\n- `AssignHousehold` still computes `householdId` (used for household-size counting and membership derivations) \u2014 only its role in duplicate detection was removed. Javadocs updated accordingly.\n\nThe previously-failing behaviour tests (Cp10 same-name/postcode/different-phone \u2192 soft match not 409; Cp28/Cp52 64-hex key; Cp35 Soundex soft-match) are now green, and the existing collision/household/membership tests continue to pass.",
